# L §4.4 (tally 2.1.8 R13, X1; c3n t2): windows each takes only the unknown days the line's answer carries. The
# balance on 2026-03-06 carries w1 and w2 (m1, m2); m3's day w3 in May is met by the walk but never read by the
# result, so no head names it. 2.1.7's refcore ended every head with w3 = 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-03.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w1: date
input w2: date
input w3: date
input a: date
input b[d in days]: date

move m1: transfers
  on w1
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move m2: transfers
  on w2
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move m3: transfers
  on w3
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  w1 = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  w2 = window(2026-03-06, 2026-03-08) "s"
  w3 = window(2026-05-01, 2026-05-03) "s"
  a = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-02) "s"
  b[2026-03-01] = window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-02) "s"
  b[2026-03-02] = 2026-05-01 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask t1: bal(konto, 2026-03-06)
ask t2: bal(konto, 2026-03-06) windows each
=== expect
t1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a balance" (m1) ?"date within window(2026-03-06, 2026-03-08) not precise enough for a balance" (m2)
  cut 2026-01-01
t2 [w1 = 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-06, w2 = 2026-03-06]: 200.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
t2 [w1 = 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-06, w2 = 2026-03-07 .. 2026-03-08]: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
t2 [w1 = 2026-03-07, w2 = 2026-03-06]: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
t2 [w1 = 2026-03-07, w2 = 2026-03-07 .. 2026-03-08]: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input a is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input b is read by nothing
